# Keep line endings LF everywhere, in the repo and in the working tree.
#
# This project is edited from two places at once: a Linux sandbox that writes
# LF, and Windows where core.autocrlf would otherwise rewrite every file to
# CRLF on checkout. Without this, each side keeps "changing" files the other
# side just wrote, and diffs fill up with invisible whitespace churn.
#
# Python, Tk and Windows all read LF happily, so pinning to LF costs nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...with one exception. cmd.exe parses batch files by seeking through them
# byte by byte, and with LF-only endings it can mis-read labels, `goto` and
# `( ... )` blocks. A one-line launcher survives it; the same file with a
# `pause` and an `if` in it may not, and it would fail only after a fresh
# clone -- working on the machine that wrote it and broken everywhere else.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
